WEBVTT

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:37.410
Strike!

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:43.370
Hi, Coach!

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.250
Mrs. Hanai!

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:46.620
And...?

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:50.040
Good day! I'm Mrs. Abe.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.840
I'm sorry I couldn't be there for the first game.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:54.510
Mrs. Abe!

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:57.010
Nice to meet you! Thanks for coming.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:01.140
Hanai, I'm leaving you in charge for a bit, okay?

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:02.470
Okay!

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.720
You went to see his little brother's game?

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:05.520
Exactly.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:08.400
I'm counting on you, Captain!

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.230
Shit! Just shut up and go!

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.360
That's your mother, Abe?

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:14.230
Yeah.

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:15.530
She came to watch?

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:16.900
She must really like baseball, then.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:17.780
Yeah.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:19.570
I knew that Hanai's family liked baseball, though.

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:20.120
Yeah.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:24.040
My mom and dad went to the Hatsukari Stadium yesterday.

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:25.580
Was there a good game or something?

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.290
My parents went to Oomiya today to watch a baseball game.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:31.710
What a coincidence! My parents also said that they were going to Oomiya!

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.210
It's not a coincidence!

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.800
We split the parents up into groups to film the games in our block!

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:38.590
That scared the life out of me!

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:39.760
What are you angry about?

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:43.470
Why don't you know anything about filming the games?

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.100
I haven't heard anything.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:45.930
Your parents told you, didn't they!?

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:47.230
You're too close. Move.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.230
Hanai, you're close with your parents, aren't you?

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:52.020
No, I'm not!

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:55.730
So I keep the display like this and switch it on only when recording, right?

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:56.990
Yes.

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.950
The sun's strong here,

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:02.950
so don't forget to consume enough salt and liquids; also, beware of heatstrokes.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:05.540
We're experts at observing baseball games.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:06.740
We've been doing it for years.

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:08.750
Ah, that's right.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.920
You've been around baseball since elementary school.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:11.620
So...

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.000
Yes?

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:15.380
Have you also been playing baseball since elementary school, Coach?

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:18.210
Mixed in with the boys in the Little League or something?

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:21.220
I was in a regional club during elementary school.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.260
In middle school, I was on the softball team.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:25.430
You went to Nishiura for high school, right?

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:26.470
So you played softball there after all?

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:27.150
No.

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:28.640
I was the manager of the baseball club.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:29.600
Out!
I was the manager of the baseball club.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.020
The manager!?

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:34.400
It would be weird if I said it was a waste, but really!?

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:38.280
You see, my son told me that your fungo is really good,

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.400
but he wonders where you practiced.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.780
"Really good," is it?

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.620
Like an expert!

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.160
That makes me happy.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.120
I did it during high school.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.910
So managers also help with practice?

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:54.290
People who set up training schedules and such are called managers as well, right?

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:58.550
It's nothing that impressive,

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:01.880
but the advising teacher was someone who had never played baseball before.

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:03.430
Plus, we didn't have many players,

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:06.300
so I helped hit practice balls infield and pitched during batting practice every day.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:09.850
Isn't Mr. Shiga the advising teacher?

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:12.440
Yes, he is. The old one transferred.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:13.480
Here you go.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.810
Thank you!

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:17.230
This used to be a rubber ball baseball team after all.

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:19.820
It was completely different from how it is now.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.660
It's chilled and very refreshing!

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:29.450
I'm glad.

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:32.160
Well, I'm going back, then.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:36.290
I'll be over there, so if there's anything you need, call me on my cellphone.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:37.790
Okay.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:39.960
All right.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:43.840
A rubber ball baseball team, huh?

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:47.140
If I remember correctly, they became a regular baseball team last year.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:49.640
I wonder how many years it's been since she became the manager.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:52.770
It's a bit surprising that she chose to be the manager,

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:54.980
but seeing as she's going through the trouble of reviving the baseball club,

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.940
it must be very enjoyable for her.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:58.690
Out!

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:03.650
But why haven't any of the old team members shown up?

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:07.780
It'd be nice if they dropped by with some refreshments while Momoe's at it.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:12.410
I wonder how her old team members are doing now.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.880
I want to ask her so many things, but I guess it's too soon for that.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:20.500
When the tournament's over, I'll organize a drinking party.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:28.180
Strike!

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.140
Three up, three down!

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:31.060
Was that a screwball?

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:32.600
Maybe. He's a southpaw after all.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:35.060
What is the pitcher's year?

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:37.230
Second year.

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:40.900
The shortstop is third year, and the third baseman and catcher are first years.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.940
The rest are all second years.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.900
The catcher is a first year?

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:48.360
Hey...

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:49.160
Nice pitching!

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:50.990
Is that the catcher?

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.290
He has a strong presence.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:55.660
His batting average in the first game was 1.000.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.420
1.000?

00:05:58.420 --> 00:05:59.710
Out of how many at bats?

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:01.040
There were extra innings, right?

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:01.790
Six out of six.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:04.090
He also made the game-winning hit.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:05.470
Mihashi!

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.800
You weighed yourself today, right?

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:11.180
How many kilos?

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:15.680
Um... Fifty...

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.100
It's coming back up, isn't it?

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:19.060
Yeah!

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:19.520
Until the next game, your goal is to gain back as much weight as you can, okay?

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:20.610
What's his RBI?

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.110
I haven't checked that far.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.110
Let's go ask Shinooka.

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:23.900
Next game?

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:23.940
This time we have a one week gap,

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:25.110
Shinooka!

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:26.190
What?

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:26.400
The catcher of Sakitama.
This time we have a one week gap,

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:27.490
but we'll only have three days for the next one and one day in between

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.360
What was his RBI for the previous game?

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:30.870
Eh...

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:32.870
There won't be time to regain your weight, then.

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.040
I-I see.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:37.540
But seriously, it's pretty frightening...

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:42.340
If he drops three kilos every game, he'd disappear in no time!

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:46.420
He's going through some pretty intensive things in training every day,

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.090
but I guess a real game is special after all.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.130
I'll drink a lot and eat a lot.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:52.760
From now on, it won't be about just winning the game.

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:58.730
To aim for the top with him, we have to figure out an easier way to win.

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:01.440
If you drink too much, you won't be able to eat!

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.820
Be careful before meals!

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:08.650
About how tall is your father?

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:12.780
His height? I don't know...

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:15.160
Um, about this high...

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.200
Looks to be about 175cm.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.670
I-I'm sorry.

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:24.130
Mihashi's mother is around 160cm, so...

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:27.760
I guess he'll grow to an average height as well.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:31.430
Growing smoothly, doing regular muscle training...

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:35.720
I think if you continue like this, you'll be able to throw like that pitcher.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:39.350
Did he just say something about me?

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:44.230
The speed of your pitch may not come naturally,
but don't push yourself too hard.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:48.900
What?

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:50.990
Abe is...

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:53.160
What is it!? Say it already!

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:00.910
If you cover your mouth while talking,

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:02.580
I can't understand a thing you're saying, can I!?

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:05.210
He ran away.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:06.960
Wow, he got five RBIs last game!
He ran away.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:09.710
He remembers it well.

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:14.430
It's true that I said he doesn't need speed during training camp.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:17.470
And even now I still think so.

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:20.890
Is it wrong to try to raise the speed of his pitch?

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:24.520
Out!

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:28.480
With just control and breaking balls, how many rounds do you think you'll make it through?

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:35.450
I think it would be great if Mihashi could throw fastballs since he said he wants to.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:41.000
But I won't let him lose his control over his fastball or nine-section pitching.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:44.460
We've got to proceed carefully. Very carefully.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.750
Hey, Abe.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:50.710
Just now, were you yelling about something?

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.550
No, not really.

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:55.800
I might have raised my voice. Why?

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:59.600
Well... I got a little scared.

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:01.560
Scared of what?

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:04.770
Of what? Well, of your voice.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:09.360
During a game it doesn't matter, but when we're just talking...

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:11.650
Even if you're just laughing...

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:15.910
When your voice is loud, I get scared and become timid.

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:17.590
I might have sounded like a wimp there.

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:19.330
Even when I'm laughing!?

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:23.950
Mihashi is the same too and immediately gets scared of your loud voice!

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:27.540
I want to say that, but I can't...

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.590
It feels like he'd get angry!

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:31.420
Strike!

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:37.380
I thought Abe didn't expect much speed from my pitch.

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:40.850
You'll be able to throw like that pitcher.

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:47.520
It went through!

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:48.850
Nice batting!

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:52.690
Mr. Cleanup, your commentary on the current at bat, please!

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:56.820
The pitch was around 125 km/h,
which makes it easy to hit.

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:57.860
I see!

00:09:57.860 --> 00:09:59.620
Then would you hit it as well, Mr. Cleanup?

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:01.410
Well, wouldn't you?

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:02.620
And really, Mizutani, you're annoying!

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:04.080
Why?

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.210
You're being too gleeful about it.

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:08.080
I see...

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:09.540
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:13.460
So... if I pushed myself, I could be faster...

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:19.800
I have to push myself.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:21.800
I have to try much, much hard-

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:24.310
Be honest and tell me what you were looking at just now.

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:26.850
Just now?

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:28.230
I-I...?

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:28.770
Pi...

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:32.190
Not the pitcher...

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:37.650
Is there some point in lying!?

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:41.780
You've seen the data that Shinooka made, didn't you?

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:42.320
Yeah.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:45.790
It took her an incredible amount of time and effort to make that list of every at bat, you know.

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:52.040
She went through the trouble of making something so difficult because it'll help us win.

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:53.790
Y-Yeah.

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:58.800
Data and videos are useful too, but today we can see it for ourselves.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:01.260
So what should you really be looking at?

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:14.650
I definitely won't yell.

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:17.610
Become like stone.

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:20.650
I can still hold out.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:22.740
Still.

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:31.290
The ba...

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:34.590
The b-batters!

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:36.590
Exactly! The batters!

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:40.090
Oops, my voice got loud again.

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:41.510
Speak normally...

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:46.140
The pitcher doesn't matter, so watch the batters, okay?

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:48.020
Okay, I-I got it!

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.560
It got through!

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:52.980
I get it! My loud voice was the problem!

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:57.110
Bottom of the second inning. Sakitama High School to bat.

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:57.610
Fifth batter. Catcher: Number 2, Sakura.

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:59.150
It's just the beginning.

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:01.030
The batter is just a first year!

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:03.030
It'll go through!

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:05.070
Out!

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:08.040
Wow, what a fine play.

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:10.300
His 1.000 record ends there.

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:12.580
His record of consecutive hits is over,

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:14.420
but he still hasn't been struck out.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:18.420
While he's a big guy, he has very precise control of the bat.

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:19.550
Nice, shortstop!

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:20.050
Nice pitching!

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:22.420
All right! I managed to end that outrageous record!

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:23.510
Nice, shortstop!

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:24.300
Nice, me!

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:24.640
Sixth batter. Center: Number 8, Kamimura.

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:27.220
I'm sorry. I ended up out.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:30.640
It's okay, Daichi. It'd be odd if you didn't get an out about now, right?

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:34.100
Even if you strike out for the rest of the game,
you'll still have a .500 batting average.

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:36.610
Well, striking out for the rest of the game is...

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:40.070
Did I say something arrogant?

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:42.360
No, it's not like that! I wasn't trying to back-talk!

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:43.030
We know...

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:47.410
If I'm careless, it's possible to strike out for the remaining at bats, isn't it!?

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:49.330
I'm sorry! I was being arrogant!

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:51.750
I want to purify my corrupted mind!

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:53.330
What should I do!?

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:55.790
For now, how about washing that filthy face?

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:56.290
Right away!

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:58.210
Thank you very much!

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:00.250
He's a serious and good guy.

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:03.130
He's good-looking and absurdly good at baseball.

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:04.300
It's just...

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:06.930
He's extremely stupid.

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:12.890
Daichi is great, but I guess this is as far as we can go.

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:15.020
Since I continued baseball on my own,

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:18.650
being able to win one game in my last year is enough of a reward.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.360
It's all thanks to you, Daichi.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:21.570
I feel refreshed!

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:22.860
Hurry up and put on your guard.

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:23.360
Yes!

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:32.040
They caught up to them in the bottom of the ninth inning!

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:33.910
How twisted is this game!?

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:35.620
Since we've gotten this far, let's win!

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:36.370
Yeah!

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:38.170
Go after the ball until the end!

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:39.040
Yeah!

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:40.040
All right!

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:42.380
Extra innings. Twice in a row.

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:44.170
What are you happy about!?

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:47.380
It's Iwatsuki West that should be happy about not being sent home.

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:51.890
But extra innings mean you can be in the stadium longer.

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:56.140
I wanted it to be decided by the ninth inning.

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:58.770
The extra innings are tough on my shoulder.

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:02.820
What a selfish person I am!

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:05.030
Just because I'm having fun...

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:05.440
Hey!

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:07.530
Why can't I think about others!?

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:07.900
I said, "Hey!"

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:08.990
My heart is corrupted!

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:09.570
Daichi!

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:10.950
Just because I'm complaining doesn't mean your heart is corrupted.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.450
I'm sorry!

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:12.990
Just because I'm complaining doesn't mean your heart is corrupted.

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:14.790
I'm sorry!

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:15.540
Just because I'm complaining doesn't mean your heart is corrupted.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:20.790
Besides, I'd prefer playing extra innings if it means we can win!

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:22.590
Really?

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:24.920
Yeah! So hit it, okay?

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:28.260
Yes!

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:32.430
Wow!

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:33.310
There it goes...

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:43.110
A walk-off home run!

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:46.070
An out-of-field walk-off home run in an extra inning.

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:47.400
So flashy...

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:48.570
Yeah.

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:50.990
That guy... is a first year, right?

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:52.620
Amazing distance.

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:55.410
Even if I lose as a batter,

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:57.500
if we win the game, then it's my win!

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:59.120
Incredible!

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:03.000
There are a lot of great players I don't know.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:05.000
If we can just hold him back,
there won't be a problem.

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:07.510
When it comes to batters, he's the only good one.

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:11.010
If it comes down to it,
we can just walk him every time.

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:16.770
Are you against walking him?

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:19.270
Not at all!

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:23.190
What I hate the most is giving up a hit!

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:29.950
I guess that's true.

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:34.320
Good game!

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:38.080
What I hate the most is giving up a hit.

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:44.630
Giving up a hit and having the team lose...

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:45.590
I hate it!

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:50.800
It's not allowed?

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:52.680
No, it's not.

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:56.390
If the cheering squad were to be recognized as a club,

00:15:56.390 --> 00:16:00.640
I would, without hesitation, allow you guys to be absent from class, so I know it sounds strange.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:04.770
But you know, high school baseball is very strict, right?

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:05.940
That's right.

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:10.490
If you were to skip class and go to cheer for the team and someone complained,

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:13.780
and the baseball team was bad-mouthed, that wouldn't be your intention either, would it?

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:15.870
No.

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:18.120
Let's stick to the rules!

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:21.540
I think that will be in your best interest too.

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:22.080
Yes.

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:24.170
Hamada.

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:27.920
The rooting for Nishiura during the game against Tousei was perfect!

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:29.880
Everyone is thankful for it.

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:32.840
They won't let it end when you're not around to cheer for them.

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:34.340
Nishiura! Go! Go! Go! Go! Go!

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:34.800
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:35.140
Nishiura! Go! Go! Go! Go! Go!

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:35.640
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:36.010
Nishiura! Go! Go! Go! Go! Go!

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:36.510
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:36.890
Nishiura! Go! Go! Go! Go! Go!

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:37.350
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:37.720
Nishiura! Go! Go! Go! Go! Go!

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:38.720
It's hot!

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:39.100
I'm done for! Damn!

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:39.970
And the distance we ran wasn't even that long...

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:41.600
I'm done for! Damn!

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:44.270
We're meeting up at 10:00 am!

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:46.060
Don't waste any time!

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:49.400
It's already soaking wet.

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:50.530
Feels gross!

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:51.690
Tajima!

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:55.200
If you're going to take off your boxers,
do it where no one can see you!

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:57.450
Don't make me say it over and over again!

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.240
The neighbors will report you to the police!

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:03.080
But there are mosquitoes flying in the dugout, so I can't take my dick out!

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:06.580
Looks like you're having a hard time.

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:10.460
I-I'm not...

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:13.470
You're panting a lot, though.

00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:16.430
Why do you always try to hide such obvious things?

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:19.100
This feels great!

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:24.980
How stupid can you get!?

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:26.230
It's free to use.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:26.850
What's up?

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:29.940
Everyone's worn out under the blazing sun.

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:31.020
It's really not a big deal!

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:31.820
Oh, right...

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:35.490
But when you consider your stamina back then,

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:37.320
you understand how badly out of shape you are, right?

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:41.240
For the 1500 meters, it's fine if you come in after Tajima.

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:49.350
You did <i>not</i> need to do that again!

00:17:49.350 --> 00:17:55.760
We got some bananas from Abe and Hanai's mothers,
so today we'll have banana protein juice!

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:56.420
Gimme!

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:01.140
Go after changing your undershirt!

00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:01.680
All right!

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:05.980
I feel like it's not just the loudness of my voice.

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:09.650
Something more on a fundamental level isn't getting through.

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:13.320
Well then, let's start by going over the game we watched.

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:14.780
First, fielding.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.690
In any case, we have to keep an eye out for that fifth batter.

00:18:16.690 --> 00:18:18.530
Not just the fifth batter.

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:21.030
The first through the fourth got on base often too.

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:23.490
Half of the runs had nothing to do with the fifth batter.

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:26.370
The fourth batter also scored two runs.

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:28.410
The run in the ninth inning was also hit by the fourth batter.

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:31.130
Okay. In summary...

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:32.750
Their only left-hander is the ninth batter,

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:35.260
so be aware of that during fielding practice on the left side.

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:37.050
Izumi, Suyama, and Mizutani!

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:38.220
All right!

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:42.180
Sakitama is weak when it comes to advancing bases, so improve your pickoff timing.

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:44.760
Mihashi, Abe, Sakaeguchi, and Suyama.

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:45.890
Got it!

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:47.140
The rest applies to everyone!

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:52.360
When fielding, make sure to work together in dealing with bunts and fly balls!

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:53.400
That's all.

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:53.980
Okay.

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:55.360
Let's go with that as our training menu.

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:56.440
All right!

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:58.110
Then next is their offense!

00:18:58.110 --> 00:19:01.530
If we're going with this batting order, we have to get Tajima on base first.

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:03.070
Then you'll make the hits, right?

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:04.240
I know!

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:05.490
Take your advancing role seriously!

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:06.080
I am!

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:09.210
The pitcher is left-handed, so the runner on first base should look out.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:11.710
The catcher's pickoff got my attention.

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:14.000
You're scared of that overaction?

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:15.880
Well, he trapped two runners, didn't he?

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:17.550
The runners made both of those mistakes, didn't they?

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:19.420
There's no guarantee we won't make a mistake as well.

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:22.840
With a runner on first and third base, it's annoying if he keeps on throwing those pickoffs.

00:19:22.840 --> 00:19:24.890
And that's why they couldn't get set up even once.

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:26.680
Now that you mention it, that might be true.

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:29.350
Well, the base coach should watch out for that.

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:29.810
For the next game, there's nothing you can do except run, you know.

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:31.730
Confirm where the ball is and be sure to tell the others!

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:33.310
Yeah, I'll run all the way round!

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:34.310
Anything else?

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:35.820
Yeah, I have one.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:37.980
I want us to aim for a shut-out.

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:43.110
Going along with Sakitama into extra innings? No way.

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:44.780
Even nine innings is too long.

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:49.250
If we continue down this path, we're going to fall apart, starting with Mihashi.

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:51.000
I thought about it for a long time, but in order to have him last,

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:52.420
I-I...

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:53.250
I thought about it for a long time, but in order to have him last,

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:56.340
I think it's best to end the game quickly.

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:57.500
I guess...

00:19:57.500 --> 00:19:58.760
That might be true, but...

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:02.130
"I can still pitch," right?

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:03.260
Mihashi would say that!

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:04.720
Abe, you don't sound like him!

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:07.810
You know, if we're aiming for it, then I want to do it.

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:09.970
It's normally easier that way.

00:20:09.970 --> 00:20:12.060
That's why I'm saying let's go for it.

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:13.560
Yeah, it might be a good idea.

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:19.070
Sakitama scored a lot of runs, but they also gave away a lot at the same time.

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:22.240
In the first game, they allowed seven runs up until the seventh inning.

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:23.320
And five runs in the second game.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:23.650
Really?

00:20:23.650 --> 00:20:24.570
If we don't give away any runs, it won't be that difficult!

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:26.530
I see.

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:27.080
If we don't give away any runs, it won't be that difficult!

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:30.160
Moreover, since I don't think they've got our data,

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:32.500
it'll be effective if we start bringing in runs early on.

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:34.960
We can even give them a shock that way.

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:37.750
Five runs in the first inning would be great,

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:40.380
but I think it'll be fine if we manage to score two runs per inning.

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:44.510
But this calculation only works if we don't give up any runs ourselves, right?

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:45.650
So what do we do about the fifth batter?

00:20:45.650 --> 00:20:47.300
We're going to walk him.

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:49.970
All his at bats?

00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:51.310
I'll sit at his second at bat.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:53.270
We might make him walk in the end, but...

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:57.480
If we need to face him at some point, it's better to have pitched once already.

00:20:57.900 --> 00:21:01.280
So showing the opponent that we're walking their fifth batter will weaken their motivation.

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:02.000
Yeah.

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:05.800
Sakitama's fifth batter is their emotional support.

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:09.580
If we don't let him challenge us, their team will get discouraged.

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:12.790
Then everyone else's movements will get dull.

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:14.500
I kind of understand that...

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:16.580
But can we manage that?

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:19.130
He's really observant.

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:22.550
Creating a positive atmosphere in your own team's dugout is something everyone thinks of.

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:24.630
But to make the opposing team discouraged...

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:26.800
Is that really a first year's way of thinking?

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:28.050
Oh yeah, Coach.

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:29.140
Yes?

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:30.850
Can you throw screwballs?

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:34.850
I used to throw them before, so I think it'll work out somehow.

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:36.160
I'll go prepare for it right away!

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:36.980
Awesome!

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:37.770
Seriously!?

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:39.730
I've never hit a screwball before.

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:43.860
D-Does anyone have anything left to say?

00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:46.700
There's no reason to disagree with Abe.

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:49.030
Let's just try our best.

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:49.530
Yeah!

00:21:49.530 --> 00:21:51.080
If we can do it, it'd be amazing!

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:51.780
It's getting...

00:21:51.780 --> 00:21:53.120
...interesting!

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:55.200
Are we going to do it?

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:57.920
Are we really going to aim for a shut-out!?

00:21:57.920 --> 00:22:01.290
Doesn't that mean that as the cleanup hitter, I have to produce good results!?

00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:02.380
Let's go for it!

00:22:02.380 --> 00:22:03.340
All right!

00:22:03.340 --> 00:22:04.300
We've got four days left!

00:22:04.300 --> 00:22:06.380
Let's practice with that goal in mind!

00:22:06.380 --> 00:22:06.920
Yeah!

00:22:08.890 --> 00:22:10.300
We're going for a shut-out!

00:22:10.300 --> 00:22:11.760
Yeah!

00:23:42.900 --> 00:23:45.440
At last, the third-round game has begun.

00:23:45.440 --> 00:23:49.610
Nishiura's objective today is to get a shut-out.

00:23:49.610 --> 00:23:51.950
For that purpose, we must get a lot of runs.

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:56.580
In other words, we need our cleanup hitter, Hanai, to be a hero.

00:23:56.910 --> 00:23:59.290
We're expecting a lot from Hanai's batting.

00:23:59.290 --> 00:24:03.210
But for some reason, Hanai looks restless.

00:24:03.210 --> 00:24:04.880
Maybe it's just my imagination?

00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:07.040
Next time:

00:24:07.040 --> 00:24:08.630
The Third-Round Game.

00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:10.840
Hanai, you can become a hero.
